 "content_notes": "Closed at trial: Dzhokhar Tsarnaev was convicted on all 30 counts in April 2015 and sentenced to death; the sentence was vacated in 2020, reinstated by the Supreme Court in 2022 and remains under appeal (stated as 'appeals continue'). The bombing, the finish line, the victims, injuries, the carjacking, the shootout, the standoff and any weapon or explosion are never depicted: the bombing is one spoken line, the toll a typed card in a quiet room, the shootout a card over a dark street with police lights. Victims are named only on the memorial card; the memorial is the last spoken line. Tsarnaev is only a dark shape inside the boat and, in court, an anonymous rim-lit silhouette (not a likeness, never a photo recreation), never posed heroically; none of his words, the note's content or his beliefs are quoted. The homeowner is a generic, unnamed figure (not a likeness); the officers are generic, with no insignia and no weapons. The boat, trailer, house, yard, street and city are generic drawings with no name, number, sign or logo (no boat name, no real street). Every card is our own typed graphic; no real police, court or FBI material is imitated. No dialogue is invented. Legal status verified 2026-10-12.",
